{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Its lamps, the lamps of the arrangement.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it added 'the lamps of the arrangement' in order to explain that 'its lamps' are the seven that Aaron and his sons would arrange between the evenings, and it comes to teach that one may neither add to them nor subtract from them. And it is further possible to say that Scripture alludes that the seven lamps correspond to the seven wandering stars, which are lamps in the heavens; therefore it added 'the lamps of the arrangement,' to explain that the lamps of the pure lampstand correspond to the lamps of the supernal arrangement. And I have already explained this in the section of ויקחו לי תרומה." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah concerning the matter of the lampstand, I have already written it in its place there, in the fourth way."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:53.979707656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}